---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[])"
---
CLI and TUI for GP2040-CE gamepads: status, input modes, profiles

Usage: gamepadii [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  status     The pad on USB: input mode (with a confidence), USB ids, bus and port
  info       Firmware, board, memory, input mode, profiles and boot buttons. Needs web-config; in a gamepad mode the control channel takes the pad there and back
  backup     Save every readable setting to one JSON file. Needs web-config; in a gamepad mode the control channel takes the pad there and back. With control channel v1.6, the file also has the saved config as one blob, for `restore`
  restore    Write the config blob of a backup file back to the pad, over the control channel (needs v1.6). This writes all the settings to flash
  reboot     Restart the pad into gamepad mode, web-config or BOOTSEL, then wait for it on USB and check what came back. Needs web-config, or the control channel in a gamepad mode
  mode       Switch the input mode, or with no MODE show the current one and the choices. In a gamepad mode it uses the control channel, or else says which buttons to press and waits
  webconfig  Get the pad into web-config and print its URL; in a gamepad mode it reboots it over the control channel, or else says which buttons to press and waits
  profile    Pin-mapping profiles on the pad
  leds       The per-button RGB LEDs: animation, brightness, colours and the custom theme, or the lights profile on main firmware. Over the control channel when the firmware has the LED commands (no reboot); else from web-config, where stock firmware doesn't show the animation or brightness (in a gamepad mode the control channel takes the pad there and back)
  input      Read the buttons live (needs control channel v1.7 of the gamepadii firmware): the GPIOs pressed now, with their action and key, and the gamepad state
  log        The pad's log of its last 64 events, live (needs control channel v1.8 of the gamepadii firmware)
  tui        The terminal UI: the pad, its input modes and profiles, web-config and backups. `gamepadii` with no command opens it on a terminal
  display    The pad's OLED display
  setup      One-time setup of this machine
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` and `leds` only
          
          [default: human]

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

      --no-channel
          Don't use the USB control channel (the gamepadii firmware's): only web-config and button presses

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
